    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode, falling back to the city table.\n\n**`Locality.java`** \u2014 kept the existing `of(String city)` untouched and added two small, cohesive methods plus a postcode-range table:\n- `of(String city, String postcode)` \u2014 resolves by postcode range first, then falls back to `of(city)`.\n- `byPostcode(String postcode)` \u2014 validates a 4-digit postcode and maps it to a region via `REGION_POSTCODES` (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099), returning `null` when absent/out of range.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the one `locality` mapping expression now passes the postcode: `Locality.of(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())`.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** Only two files touched. The existing `of(city)` and the mapper's other methods were left unchanged; new behaviour lives in new small methods inside `Locality`, a class whose surrounding complexity (`WMC_other`) is minimal, so the added logic doesn't pay for a large class. Known cities still resolve to the same region, while cities sharing a name are now disambiguated by postcode \u2014 exactly what the two new tests assert.",
