    "probe_text": "Here is every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, in the order it executes. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`.\n\n## Gating (before the method body runs)\n\n1. **Security filter chain** \u2014 when `petclinic.security.enable=true`, the request must be authenticated (HTTP Basic, JDBC-backed). When `false`, all requests are permitted.\n2. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole('ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN')\")`** \u2014 caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (enforced only when security is enabled).\n\n## Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`\n\nAny failure below \u2192 **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n\n3. **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/apostrophe/hyphen).\n4. **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (as above, allows a trailing dot).\n5. **address** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (must contain a non-whitespace char).\n6. **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (non-whitespace char required).\n7. **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` (intl `+`, leading-0 national, or bare national), **plus** custom field-level `@E164NationalLength` (after normalizing to E.164, national-digit count must match the country code: `+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210; unknown codes pass).\n8. **email** \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional/nullable).\n9. **postcode** \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^\\\\d{4}$\")` (optional; exactly 4 digits when present).\n10. **Class-level `@ValidPostcode`** \u2014 cross-field: resolves a region from the *city* (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) and requires the postcode to fall in that range. Passes if postcode blank, city unknown, or postcode not 4 digits.\n\n## Mapping + entity normalization (MapStruct `toOwner`, applied in the setters)\n\n11. **email** lowercased.\n12. **address** normalized: trimmed, whitespace collapsed, UPPERCASED, abbreviations expanded (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n13. **telephone** normalized to **E.164** (strip non-digits; keep `+`+digits, else drop one leading `0` and prefix `+61`).\n\n## Controller business logic (in order)\n\n14. **Registration date** \u2014 use the supplied date or `LocalDate.now()`, then roll forward with `BusinessDay.adjust` (Sat/Sun \u2192 next Monday); set on the owner.\n15. **Load all owners once** \u2014 `clinicService.findAllOwners()` (`findAll()`), reused for all checks below.\n16. **Throttle check** \u2014 if \u2265100 existing owners share this registration date \u2192 return **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS** (no save).\n17. **Conflict check** \u2014 if any existing owner has the same `identityKey` (`telephone|email|`), OR \u226550 existing owners are in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 return **409 CONFLICT** (no save).\n18. **Set `namesakeCount`** = count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n19. **Set `householdMemberCount`** = 1 + existing owners with same last name AND same address.\n20. **Set `customerCode`** = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN = (existing owners in same city) + 1, zero-padded.\n\n## Persistence and post-save\n\n21. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 `@Transactional` `ownerRepository.save()` (plain insert; IDENTITY id generated).\n22. **`@PrePersist`** safety net \u2014 defaults `registrationDate` to now if null (already set, so normally a no-op).\n23. **`@PostPersist`** (`OwnerAuditListener`) \u2014 writes an AUDIT log line: `owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026`.\n24. **Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`**, computing derived read-only fields: `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `membershipNumber`.\n25. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** = (existing owners with same registration date) > 80.\n26. **Set `Location` header** `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes\n\n- There is **no** password encoding, event publishing, or email/notification sending on this path.\n- All uniqueness/throttle checks are done **in-memory over `findAll()`** \u2014 no DB unique constraint or `existsBy` query \u2014 so they are race-prone under concurrency.\n- `Owner.getIdentityKey()` builds `telephone|email|` and does **not** include the household id, despite the `OwnerDto.identityKey` documentation suggesting otherwise.\n- `householdMemberCount` is computed and stored but never mapped into the response DTO."
